INT. CURLING CLUB - LOCKER ROOM - EVENING

Wet wool. Steam. The thump of stones through a wall.

A YOUNG WOMAN sits on the bench in her stocking feet, broom across her knees. Twenties, red parka, a bruise on her cheekbone from a fall. She stares at nothing.

Coach HJALMAR ODUYA-KRISTENSEN (60s, club blazer, whistle) stands at the door with a clipboard. He does not speak. He taps the clipboard against his thigh.

At the far end, a veteran, MAUREEN "MO" DELACROIX-ABARA (40s, gray-blonde braid) tightens a boot. She doesn't look up either.

The young woman bends. Unlaces one shoe. Laces it again. Same shoe.

HJALMAR
Five minutes.

The young woman nods.

MO
(to Hjalmar)
Leave her.

HJALMAR
She has a stone to throw.

MO
She has a minute.

Hjalmar studies the young woman. She picks up the broom. Puts it down. Picks up a towel and presses it to her cheek.

A horn sounds in the hallway.

Mo stands. Offers her hand. The young woman looks at it, then up at her face.

MO (CONT'D)
Brynja.

BRYNJA
(rising)
I'm fine.

She isn't. She takes the hand anyway.

Hjalmar steps aside from the door. The three of them walk out together, Brynja in the middle, broom over her shoulder, jaw set.
